<Legal lang="en" doc="privacy" title="Privacy policy" updated="8 October 2026" description="What humcase.com and the Humcase app do with your data, and your rights.">
  <div class="summary">
    <h2>In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The website sets no cookies and uses no analytics or advertising.</li>
      <li>The Humcase app keeps your data on your computer. There is no account, and we never receive your cases.</li>
      <li>If you turn on an AI or dictation feature, the text or audio goes from your computer straight to the provider you chose, with your own key.</li>
      <li>If you sign up for release news, your address is used only to tell you about new versions, until you unsubscribe.</li>
      <li>If you write to us, your message is used only to answer you.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>The data controller is the publisher of humcase.com, named in the <a href="/legal/notice/">legal notice</a>. For any question about your data: <a href="mailto:contact@humcase.com">contact@humcase.com</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The website</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted by Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site against attacks, Cloudflare processes technical connection data: IP address, browser, pages requested, date and time. Cloudflare acts on our behalf; its own practices are described in the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>The site sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and loads no analytics, advertising or social media tools. Its fonts are served from humcase.com itself. No consent banner is therefore needed.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Release news</h2>
    <p>When you sign up on the home page, we send a confirmation email to the address you typed, with the language of the page. Your address joins the list only once you click the link in that email; an unconfirmed link expires after 7 days and nothing is kept.</p>
    <p>The list and the emails are handled on our behalf by Resend, Inc. (<a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Resend privacy policy</a>). We use your address only to announce new versions of Humcase, on the basis of your consent. Every email has an unsubscribe link; you can also write to <a href="mailto:contact@humcase.com">contact@humcase.com</a>. Once you unsubscribe, we no longer email you.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>When you write to us</h2>
    <p>Messages sent to a humcase.com address are forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to the publisher’s mailbox, hosted by Google (Gmail). We use your address and your message only to answer you and follow up on the exchange, which is our legitimate interest. We keep them only as long as the exchange needs, and never share them.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Humcase app</h2>
    <p>Humcase is a local application. Your cases, projects, images and settings are stored in a folder of your computer (<code>.humcase</code> in your user folder). The app needs no account, sends no usage statistics and contains no tracker. We have no access to your data.</p>
    <h3>Optional AI and dictation features</h3>
    <p>Some features call an online provider, only when you turn them on and enter your own API key:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Structure, Sprout and dictation cleanup: the service you choose (Cerebras, OpenAI, Groq, OpenRouter, or an address you set) receives the case’s text, up to 4,000 words for Sprout;</li>
      <li>Ask Humcase: the same service receives your question, the earlier questions and answers of the conversation, up to nine sentences from each of the seven closest cases, and the title, project, nature, status and dates of your 25 most recent cases of the space;</li>
      <li>voice dictation: Deepgram;</li>
      <li>TypeSafe (Jev), to check natures, Sprout and To tidy: the title and first 300 words of the cases concerned, and for Sprout the proposed passages with up to 1,500 characters around them. What looks like a secret or an email address is removed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The content is sent from your computer to that provider, under the contract you have with it; we are not a party to it and receive nothing. A local model (Ollama, LM Studio) keeps everything on your computer.</p>
    <h3>AI agents</h3>
    <p>The agents you connect to Humcase (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, opencode…) read and write your cases on your computer. What they send online is governed by those tools and their providers.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare, Google and Resend are based in the United States. Transfers rely on the safeguards these providers offer: the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR and the French Data Protection Act, you can access your data, correct it, erase it, restrict or object to its processing, and ask for its portability. Write to <a href="mailto:contact@humcase.com">contact@humcase.com</a>; we answer within one month.</p>
    <p>You can also lodge a complaint with the CNIL, the French data protection authority (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener">cnil.fr</a>), or with the authority of your country.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will update this policy when the site or the app changes what it does with data, for example when it adds a new service. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
  </section>
</Legal>
